00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,200
Circle

2
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:11,680
Observing circle we see

3
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:24,120
Circle center O, radius ON, diameter CD

4
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:33,230
OC, OD are also radii of circle.

5
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:39,890
CD passes through center of circle

6
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:56,000
so three points C, O, D are collinear and CO = OD

7
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:00,980
O is midpoint of CD.

8
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:08,290
Therefore, diameter length is twice radius length.

